    body = charToRaw("[{\"url\":\"ghrepos/hypertidy/ncmeta/issues/53\",\"repository_url\":\"ghrepos/hypertidy/ncmeta\",\"labels_url\":\"ghrepos/hypertidy/ncmeta/issues/53/labels{/name}\",\"comments_url\":\"ghrepos/hypertidy/ncmeta/issues/53/comments\",\"events_url\":\"ghrepos/hypertidy/ncmeta/issues/53/events\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/hypertidy/ncmeta/issues/53\",\"id\":2881094031,\"node_id\":\"I_kwDOBZkC0M6rugGP\",\"number\":53,\"title\":\"`nc_prj_to_gridmapping` not working with UTM projections?\",\"user\":{\"login\":\"MalditoBarbudo\",\"id\":4775311,\"node_id\":\"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3NzUzMTE=\",\"avatar_url\":\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4775311?v=4\",\"gravatar_id\":\"\",\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/MalditoBarbudo\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/MalditoBarbudo\",\"followers_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/MalditoBarbudo/followers\",\"following_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/MalditoBarbudo/following{/other_user}\",\"gists_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/MalditoBarbudo/gists{/gist_id}\",\"starred_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/MalditoBarbudo/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\"subscriptions_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/MalditoBarbudo/subscriptions\",\"organizations_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/MalditoBarbudo/orgs\",\"repos_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/MalditoBarbudo/repos\",\"events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/MalditoBarbudo/events{/privacy}\",\"received_events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/MalditoBarbudo/received_events\",\"type\":\"User\",\"user_view_type\":\"public\",\"site_admin\":false},\"labels\":[],\"state\":\"open\",\"locked\":false,\"assignees\":[],\"milestone\":null,\"comments\":12,\"created_at\":\"2025-02-26T10:37:45Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-07-29T06:47:55Z\",\"closed_at\":null,\"assignee\":null,\"author_association\":\"NONE\",\"issue_field_values\":[],\"type\":null,\"active_lock_reason\":null,\"sub_issues_summary\":{\"total\":0,\"completed\":0,\"percent_completed\":0},\"issue_dependencies_summary\":{\"blocked_by\":0,\"total_blocked_by\":0,\"blocking\":0,\"total_blocking\":0},\"body\":\"Sorry if this has been reported/asked before, I didn't find anything in the other issues or the docs.\\nSeems like when CRS is in UTM projection no mapping is available, even if UTM should be recognised as transverse mercator grid mapping if I'm not mistaken. See reprex below:\\n\\n``` r\\nlibrary(ncmeta)\\nlibrary(sf)\\n#> Linking to GEOS 3.12.1, GDAL 3.8.4, PROJ 9.3.1; sf_use_s2() is TRUE\\nlibrary(stringr)\\nst_crs(25830)$proj4string\\n#> [1] \\\"+proj=utm +zone=30 +ellps=GRS80 +towgs84=0,0,0,0,0,0,0 +units=m +no_defs\\\"\\nnc_prj_to_gridmapping(st_crs(25830)$proj4string)\\n#> Warning in prepCRS(prj): no available mapping to netcdf projection, returning\\n#> empty crs list\\n#> # A tibble: 0 × 2\\n#> # ℹ 2 variables: name <chr>, value <list>\\nfoo <- st_crs(25830)$proj4string\\nbar <- stringr::str_replace(foo, \\\"utm\\\", \\\"tmerc\\\")\\nnc_prj_to_gridmapping(bar)\\n#> # A tibble: 9 × 2\\n#>   name                             value    \\n#>   <chr>                            <list>   \\n#> 1 grid_mapping_name                <chr [1]>\\n#> 2 latitude_of_projection_origin    <dbl [0]>\\n#> 3 longitude_of_central_meridian    <dbl [0]>\\n#> 4 scale_factor_at_central_meridian <dbl [0]>\\n#> 5 false_easting                    <dbl [0]>\\n#> 6 false_northing                   <dbl [0]>\\n#> 7 semi_major_axis                  <dbl [1]>\\n#> 8 inverse_flattening               <dbl [1]>\\n#> 9 longitude_of_prime_meridian      <dbl [1]>\\n```\\n\\n<sup>Created on 2025-02-26 with [reprex v2.1.1](https://reprex.tidyverse.org)</sup>\\n\\nAm I wrong in assuming this and UTM projections are not allowed?\\n\",\"closed_by\":null,\"reactions\":{\"url\":\"ghrepos/hypertidy/ncmeta/issues/53/reactions\",\"total_count\":0,\"+1\":0,\"-1\":0,\"laugh\":0,\"hooray\":0,\"confused\":0,\"heart\":0,\"rocket\":0,\"eyes\":0},\"timeline_url\":\"ghrepos/hypertidy/ncmeta/issues/53/timeline\",\"performed_via_github_app\":null,\"state_reason\":null,\"pinned_comment\":null},{\"url\":\"ghrepos/hypertidy/ncmeta/issues/48\",\"repository_url\":\"ghrepos/hypertidy/ncmeta\",\"labels_url\":\"ghrepos/hypertidy/ncmeta/issues/48/labels{/name}\",\"comments_url\":\"ghrepos/hypertidy/ncmeta/issues/48/comments\",\"events_url\":\"ghrepos/hypertidy/ncmeta/issues/48/events\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/hypertidy/ncmeta/issues/48\",\"id\":1961802635,\"node_id\":\"I_kwDOBZkC0M507ruL\",\"number\":48,\"title\":\"Bounds are not dimensions in CF Metadata Conventions files\",\"user\":{\"login\":\"pvanlaake\",\"id\":8315731,\"node_id\":\"MDQ6VXNlcjgzMTU3MzE=\",\"avatar_url\":\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8315731?v=4\",\"gravatar_id\":\"\",\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/pvanlaake\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/pvanlaake\",\"followers_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/pvanlaake/followers\",\"following_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/pvanlaake/following{/other_user}\",\"gists_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/pvanlaake/gists{/gist_id}\",\"starred_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/pvanlaake/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\"subscriptions_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/pvanlaake/subscriptions\",\"organizations_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/pvanlaake/orgs\",\"repos_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/pvanlaake/repos\",\"events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/pvanlaake/events{/privacy}\",\"received_events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/pvanlaake/received_events\",\"type\":\"User\",\"user_view_type\":\"public\",\"site_admin\":false},\"labels\":[],\"state\":\"open\",\"locked\":false,\"assignees\":[],\"milestone\":null,\"comments\":8,\"created_at\":\"2023-10-25T16:25:55Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-07-29T06:46:12Z\",\"closed_at\":null,\"assignee\":null,\"author_association\":\"CONTRIBUTOR\",\"issue_field_values\":[],\"type\":null,\"active_lock_reason\":null,\"sub_issues_summary\":{\"total\":0,\"completed\":0,\"percent_completed\":0},\"issue_dependencies_summary\":{\"blocked_by\":0,\"total_blocked_by\":0,\"blocking\":0,\"total_blocking\":0},\"body\":\"CF Metadata Conventions use NetCDF files with a sophisticated set of conventions to ease interpretation and analysis of the data. One such convention is to include a `bounds` attribute with each dimension when the data represents cells (rather than point observations on a regular grid) to indicate the boundaries of the cell along the dimension. These bounds are included in the file as 3-D arrays for `lon` and `lat` (including the `time` dimension for reasons unknown to me) and a 2-D array for `time`, with an additional first dimension called `bnds`. As per the [CF documentation](http://cfconventions.org/Data/cf-conventions/cf-conventions-1.10/cf-conventions.html#cell-boundaries), \\\"a boundary variable is considered to be part of a coordinate variable’s metadata\\\" and it is thus not a dimension. This is made clear also by the fact that for \\\"dimension\\\" `bnds` `coord_dim == FALSE`. See below example using `tidync`:\\r\\n\\r\\n```r\\r\\n> huss <- tidync(lf[1])\\r\\n> huss\\r\\n\\r\\nData Source (1): huss_day_EC-Earth3-CC_historical_r1i1p1f1_gr_19910101-19960321_v20210113.nc ...\\r\\n\\r\\nGrids (7) <dimension family> : <associated variables> \\r\\n\\r\\n[1]   D1,D2,D0 : lat_bnds    **ACTIVE GRID** ( 976384  values per variable)\\r\\n[2]   D1,D3,D0 : lon_bnds\\r\\n[3]   D3,D2,D0 : huss\\r\\n[4]   D1,D0    : time_bnds\\r\\n[5]   D0       : time\\r\\n[6]   D2       : lat\\r\\n[7]   D3       : lon\\r\\n\\r\\nDimensions 4 (3 active): \\r\\n  \\r\\n  dim   name  length     min     max start count    dmin    dmax unlim coord_dim \\r\\n  <chr> <chr>  <dbl>   <dbl>   <dbl> <int> <int>   <dbl>   <dbl> <lgl> <lgl>     \\r\\n1 D0    time    1907 51500.  53406.      1  1907 51500.  53406.  FALSE TRUE      \\r\\n2 D1    bnds       2     1       2       1     2     1       2   FALSE FALSE     ## <<<<<<<\\r\\n3 D2    lat      256   -89.5    89.5     1   256   -89.5    89.5 FALSE TRUE      \\r\\n  \\r\\nInactive dimensions:\\r\\n  \\r\\n  dim   name  length   min   max unlim coord_dim \\r\\n  <chr> <chr>  <dbl> <dbl> <dbl> <lgl> <lgl>     \\r\\n1 D3    lon      512     0  359. FALSE TRUE  \\r\\n\\r\\n> huss$attribute |> filter(name == \\\"bounds\\\") |> unnest(value)\\r\\n# A tibble: 3 × 4\\r\\n     id name   variable value    \\r\\n  <int> <chr>  <chr>    <chr>    \\r\\n1     0 bounds time     time_bnds\\r\\n2     0 bounds lat      lat_bnds \\r\\n3     0 bounds lon      lon_bnds \\r\\n```\\r\\n\\r\\nWould it be a good idea to drop the `bnds` \\\"dimension\\\" and thus the associated grids? There should be some other mechanism to keep them on, however, such that their contents can be accessed.\\r\\n\",\"closed_by\":null,\"reactions\":{\"url\":\"ghrepos/hypertidy/ncmeta/issues/48/reactions\",\"total_count\":0,\"+1\":0,\"-1\":0,\"laugh\":0,\"hooray\":0,\"confused\":0,\"heart\":0,\"rocket\":0,\"eyes\":0},\"timeline_url\":\"ghrepos/hypertidy/ncmeta/issues/48/timeline\",\"performed_via_github_app\":null,\"state_reason\":null,\"pinned_comment\":null}]"), 
